  <!-- PROBLEM & SOLUTION -->
  <h2 style="color: #0f172a; font-size: 24px; border-bottom: 2px solid #0284c7; padding-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 40px;">
    The Problem with Mobile-to-Printer Printing
  </h2>
  <p style="font-size: 16px;">
    Most home and small business users have reliable, high-performance USB printers (like <b>Canon imageCLASS MF4800 / MF3010 / LBP2900B</b>, or <b>Epson EcoTank L3210 / L3150 / L3110</b>). However, these printers lack built-in Wi-Fi or have complicated mobile apps that frequently disconnect.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 16px;">
    To print a simple photo, Aadhaar card, bill, or PDF received on WhatsApp, users typically have to:
  </p>
  <ul style="font-size: 15px; color: #475569;">
    <li>Email the document to themselves</li>
    <li>Open WhatsApp Web on their computer</li>
    <li>Download the file onto their laptop, find it in the Downloads folder, and then print</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: #0284c7;">
    <b>Print Ofo solves this permanently:</b> You simply open the photo or PDF on your Android phone, tap <b>Share &gt; Print Ofo</b>, and it prints directly through your Windows laptop in under 2 seconds!
  </p>

